{"id":"u-fbd70651-06f5-4496-a1c5-70a62c263663","src":"community","title":"Baki Aesthetics - 4 day split x2","author":"Ryan M.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/baki-aesthetics-4-day-split-x2-202","desc":"Intermediate program focused on the baki aesthetic.  \nFocused on: Arms, Chest, Upper back, forearms and calves.\nThis program assumes you have lifted consistently before and can competently perform basic strength exercises and calisthenics.\nThis program also assumes that you have developed lats(10+ pullups), shoulders(135 OHP), and posterior chain(315 deadlifts) enough to take some focus away from them, or train them for strength instead.  If you want to increase volume for these groups, you can.\nDays 1&5 are chest and back\nDays 2&6 are legs\nDays 3&7 are arms\nDays 4&8 are accessories- If you want or need to do cardio, this is the best day for that.\nI would advise focusing on intensity, making sure you can perform the recommended amount of sets at at least 9 RPE before progressing in weight.\nMAKE SURE TO WARM UP!!  I haven’t included warmup sets in the programs but you must warmup before your first set of that muscle of the workout.  An injury is the worst thing you can do for progress.\nThe program is 8 weeks long mostly because that is what I had to do to get an 8 day cycle to fit evenly in weeks.  There is no reason for you not to repeat after the 8 weeks if you want. (A deload week isn’t needed but if you want a mental break go for it.)\nI would recommend going light the first week, staying at RPE 8 or below to make sure you know the proper form for each exercise and to help you judge which weights to use next week.","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Women's"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":1072,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-29T18:59:46.324Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Chest and Back 1","Legs 1","Arms 1","Arms 1","Chest and Back 2","Legs 2","Arms 2"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10},{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Focus on the stretch and good form"},{"n":"Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":3,"hi":6,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Overhand shoulder width grip"},{"ss":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Go all the way down, don’t lock out, especially later in the set"},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":30,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Keep tension through the whole rep, shorten ROM to push past failure"}]},{"n":"T-Bar Row","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}],"note":"Slow eccentric, stretch out at the bottom and pause, then pull up explosively"},{"n":"Chest Fly (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}],"note":"Focus on the pump, aim for an even angle to hit the whole chest"},{"n":"Pullover (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}],"note":"Focus on the stretch"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Hamstring Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":8.5,"x":3}],"note":"Used to warmup the knees for squats"},{"ss":[{"n":"High Bar Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":10},{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}],"note":"Go below parallel"},{"n":"One Leg Calf Raises","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}],"note":"Use a deficit to increase ROM, stretch all the way and go slow"},{"n":"Tibialis Raises","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":25,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":9.5,"x":3}]},{"n":"Leg Extension","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":20,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":4}]},{"n":"Shrug (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":7,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"ss":[{"n":"Bicep Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10},{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":10},{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"French Press","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10},{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":10},{"lo":8,"hi":12,"r